A||||5||Shiner||Sunroof Creak||||5
Z||000000||Shiner||11-04-1999||01:01 PM||||The Vista Vent (why did they call it THAT??)<BR>on my '87 GT creaks pretty good.  It's seals decent, but even on lightly bumpy road it creaks all the time.  And ideas on how to stop this?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-04-1999||01:25 PM||||is it only when it's open? It's probly the front hinges same as mine..... I'm working on it.... I don't really see a permanant fix but maybe some parafin on the hinges would do it. Haven't hed time to try it yet. you can't use oil or anything wet or you get a mess.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88 Fiero||11-04-1999||03:31 PM||||mine does before but not now...and mine was an addition to my car. what I did is I adjust the mounting of my latch and tighten it up...since I move the latch assembly down a little bit. it put a tight pressure on the sunroof whether it's on open or close position...it doesn't creak of rattle anymore...||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shiner||11-04-1999||11:14 PM||||It only creaks, really, when it's fully closed.  I saw something on the fiero list about bending the front tang/hing things so that they are parallel with the glass??||||reg||2
Z||000004||Carrolles||11-05-1999||07:01 AM||||The hinge tabs are supposed to be coated with plastic.  Mine did the same.  I noticed that the plastic coating had fallen off and madt the tab loose in the slot.  I got new tabs and bolts from Pontiac for about $12.00.  It is very tight now.<P>Your entire Vista Vent assembly could be loose where it attaches to the roof structure.  You need to pull the headliner to check this.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJRice||11-05-1999||09:58 AM||||You could brush some of that liquid electrical tape on the tabs to restore the plastic coating.  <P>Also, Radio Shack sells some stuff called Silicon Self Fusing Tape.  It bonds to itself so it is good for covering things, and it tends to last a while.  ||||reg||1
